   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Obvious",
     "texto": [
      "To say that something is going to happen because it is evident, use **-(으)ㄹ 게 뻔하다**: 늦다 → **늦을 게 뻔해요** (it is obvious that (he/she) will be late), 비가 오다 → **비가 올 게 뻔해요** (it is obvious that it will rain).",
      "이 날씨면 내일 비가 **올 게 뻔해요** = with this weather, it is obvious that it will rain tomorrow."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "On the other hand",
     "texto": [
      "**-(으)ㄴ 반면에** and **-는 반면에** say that something is so, and by contrast something else is different: 여름은 더**운 반면에** 겨울은 추워요 = in summer it is hot, on the other hand in winter it is cold.",
      "It is a contrast, like **-지만**, but more formal."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
